From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: arm WDT_CPUS instead of WDT0

sunxi-cubie-a7s-watchdog-autostart turned on WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART, and U-Boot
arms every watchdog it probes: initr_watchdog() walks the whole WDT uclass and starts each
device with autostart set, registering each for sysreset as well
(drivers/watchdog/wdt-uclass.c). On this board that was WDT0
(watchdog@2050000 in sun60i-a733.dtsi).

On one Cubie A7S, WDT0 reset a halted panic (panic=0) in 7 of 13 runs and
a hard hang of all eight CPUs in 1 of 2. WDT_CPUS, the watchdog in the
CPUS domain, armed from Linux with busybox devmem, reset 3 of 3 of those
panics pinned to CPU2 and one unfed timeout; BL31's PSCI SYSTEM_RESET
already resets through its SRST register (measured 2026-09-15).

Upstream disables the H6's main watchdog in the same way ("Broken on some
H6 boards").

The change:

  * A7S board DT: &wdt status = "disabled" -- U-Boot no longer binds,
    starts or registers WDT0.
  * A7S board DT: r_watchdog: watchdog@7021000 under /soc. A733 UM 8.3.5
    lists WDT_CPUS at 0x07021000 with the same registers as WDT0; UM
    Table 12-1 INTID 223 "S_WDT" gives GIC SPI 191. compatible is the WDT0
    node's; the driver matches sun55i-a523-wdt (CTRL 0x0c, CFG 0x10, MODE
    0x14, as UM 8.3.6). sunxi_wdt_probe() maps the register base, stops the
    timer and takes no clock. The clocks are those of radxa's WDT0 node, hosc =
    <&osc24M> included; nothing in U-Boot reads it.
  * CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y: `wdt dev watchdog@7021000` and `wdt stop` at the
    prompt. Linux needs a device tree that drives WDT_CPUS: a system that
    does not know it is reset about 16 s after this U-Boot boots it, and
    stopping the watchdog at the prompt is how such a system is reached.

One value that this patch does not change: sun60i-a733.dtsi gives WDT0 GIC
SPI 63, while UM Table 12-1 lists SPI 106 for the A733's WDT0. U-Boot's
watchdog driver uses no interrupt and the node is disabled here, so the
value stays as it is in the WDT0 node.

Timeout and feeding are unchanged from the autostart (16 s, the uclass's
cyclic reset). Linux keeps a watchdog it finds running (sunxi_wdt since
v6.18.53).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 27062546f48..0c7fcbd4836 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -276,3 +276,27 @@
 	pcie1v8-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
 	pcie3v3-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * The watchdog U-Boot arms (WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART) and the one Linux
+ * has to feed is WDT_CPUS. WDT0 is disabled: on one Cubie A7S it
+ * reset a halted panic 7 of 13 times and a hard hang of all CPUs 1 of 2;
+ * WDT_CPUS reset 3 of 3 of those panics on CPU2 and its own unfed timeout
+ * (measured 2026-09-15). Upstream disables the H6's main watchdog in the
+ * same way.
+ */
+&wdt {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&{/soc} {
+	/* UM 8.3.5 WDT_CPUS @ 0x07021000; UM Table 12-1 INTID 223 -> GIC SPI 191. */
+	r_watchdog: watchdog@7021000 {
+		compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-wdt",
+			     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
+		reg = <0x7021000 0x20>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 191 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&osc24M>, <&rtc CLK_OSC32K>;
+		clock-names = "hosc", "losc";
+	};
+};
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index 4ab48615d39..8929d48fb64 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ CONFIG_WDT=y
 CONFIG_WDT_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART=y
+CONFIG_CMD_WDT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
 CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_ADDR=0x0709011C
